                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash \alpha(x):\sum_{y:B} R(x, y)
            %li
              %p
                The second, third, and fourth definitions of a function are interdefinable via the following relations between
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spans"} spans
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multivalued+partial+functions"} multivalued partial functions
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    From every span one could get a multivalued partial function by defining the type family
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
